{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"kaolinite-head-wildebeest","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nCommit 7fa8102477 (2026-08-08, \"Bound malformed overlap judge calls\") bounded `judge_batch` with `output_token_limit=1024`, `structured_retry_limit=0`, `transport_attempt_limit=1`, `request_timeout_limit_s=60`. The sibling call site `judge_one` in `src/rebar/llm/overlap/judge.py` — the VOLUME site (~18 of 23 LLM calls in one measured plan review, per the module's own comment) — was not given the same bounds.\n\nMeasured consequence (local usage logs, 2026-08-06→08-11): 322 terminal `overlap-judge` failures with `finish_reason=length`, each burning 48,000 output tokens = 3 attempts (pydantic-ai `OUTPUT_RETRIES=2` default) x the 16,000 default `max_tokens` cap, ~$132 of pure waste; 20+ occurrences after the 08-08 fix landed, and 7 more reproduced during replay experiments on 2026-08-11. An overlap verdict is ~100 output tokens, so an unbounded retry ladder buys nothing.\n\n## Plan\n\nMirror `judge_batch`'s bounds onto `judge_one`'s `RunRequest` (same values, same rationale comment): `output_token_limit=1024`, `structured_retry_limit=0`, `transport_attempt_limit=1`, `request_timeout_limit_s=60`. The overlap step is advisory and already abstains on any error, so tighter bounds cannot change a review verdict — a bounded failure degrades to the same abstain as an unbounded one, at ~2% of the cost.\n\nAdd a unit test pinning the bounds on the `judge_one` request (mirroring whatever pins judge_batch's; if none pins judge_batch's, add both in one test module touch).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `judge_one` builds its `RunRequest` with `output_token_limit=1024`, `structured_retry_limit=0`, `transport_attempt_limit=1`, and `request_timeout_limit_s=60`, matching `judge_batch`. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c \"import inspect, rebar.llm.overlap.judge as j; s=inspect.getsource(j.judge_one); assert 'output_token_limit=1024' in s and 'structured_retry_limit=0' in s\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] A unit test asserts the bounds appear on the request `judge_one` submits (via a stub runner capturing the `RunRequest`). Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"judge_one and bound\" -x` passes.\n- [ ] An error path still returns the abstain verdict (existing behavior unchanged). Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"overlap and judge\" -x` passes.","id":"3939-d68c-6e99-498d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"overlap-judge: judge_one lacks the malformed-output bounds judge_batch got — 48k retry storms continue"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786471256327657001,"uuid":"a03f2cec-27aa-4793-a858-f56daebf9fe3"}